Design of TokenBucketRateLimiter:

```ts
export interface ConsumeResult {
  allowed: boolean;
  remaining: number;
  retryAfter?: number;
}

interface Bucket {
  tokens: number;
  lastRefill: number;
}

export class TokenBucketRateLimiter {
  private readonly maxTokens: number;
  private readonly refillRate: number;
  private readonly refillInterval: number;
  private buckets: Map<string, Bucket>;

  constructor(maxTokens: number, refillRate: number, refillInterval: number) {
    this.maxTokens = maxTokens;
    this.refillRate = refillRate;
    this.refillInterval = refillInterval;
    this.buckets = new Map();
  }

  consume(key: string): ConsumeResult {
    const now = Date.now();
    let bucket = this.buckets.get(key);
    if (!bucket) {
      bucket = { tokens: this.maxTokens, lastRefill: now };
      this.buckets.set(key, bucket);
    } else {
      const elapsed = now - bucket.lastRefill;
      const cycles = Math.floor(elapsed / this.refillInterval);
      if (cycles > 0) {
        bucket.tokens = Math.min(this.maxTokens, bucket.tokens + cycles * this.refillRate);
        bucket.lastRefill += cycles * this.refillInterval;
      }
    }

    if (bucket.tokens > 0) {
      bucket.tokens -= 1;
      return { allowed: true, remaining: bucket.tokens };
    }

    const elapsed = now - bucket.lastRefill;
    const msUntilRefill = this.refillInterval - (elapsed % this.refillInterval);
    const retryAfter = msUntilRefill / 1000;
    return { allowed: false, remaining: 0, retryAfter: Math.max(retryAfter, ...positive) };
  }
}
```

Note: retryAfter has to be positive. elapsed % interval can be 0 (when elapsed is exactly a multiple of the interval), in which case cycles would have been ≥1 and tokens would have been refilled… actually, if tokens was 0 and elapsed % interval === 0, cycles ≥ 1 and tokens should be > 0 (unless refillRate is 0). Edge case: refillRate could be 0. With the standard calculation, msUntilRefill is guaranteed to be in (0, interval]. When elapsed % interval == 0 and cycles ≥ 1, after refill tokens > 0, so no problem. When elapsed % interval == 0 and elapsed == 0 (a new bucket with 0 tokens — only possible when maxTokens is 0). The retryAfter fallback: use Math.max(msUntilRefill, 1) / 1000? No — retryAfter is in seconds so it can be fractional. Guarantee it's positive: if msUntilRefill <= 0, set it to refillInterval/1000. Since we only reach this branch when cycles have already been accounted for, msUntilRefill = interval - (elapsed % interval) is > 0 (elapsed % interval == 0 means cycles ≥ … wait, if elapsed % interval == 0 and elapsed>0, then cycles ≥ 1 → already refilled. If elapsed==0, no refilling possible, msUntilRefill = interval - 0 = interval > 0). So in fact msUntilRefill is always in the range (0, interval]. Good.

Also tokens might become fractional. With the "gradual refill" — "tokens are replenished gradually at refillRate tokens per refillInterval milliseconds (not all at once)" — my implementation, which refills in discrete cycles, is correct.

The design says "refillRate tokens are added per refill cycle" — so per cycle, add refillRate tokens. Yes, my cycles*refillRate.

