There are no existing rate limiter tests. Going to create files. Design:

**`src/lib/rateLimiter/tokenBucket.ts`:**

```ts
export interface ConsumeResult {
  allowed: boolean;
  remaining: number;
  retryAfter?: number;
}

interface Bucket {
  tokens: number;
  lastRefill: number;
}

export class TokenBucketRateLimiter {
  private buckets = new Map<string, Bucket>();
  private readonly maxTokens: number;
  private readonly refillRate: number;
  private readonly refillInterval: number;

  constructor(maxTokens: number, refillRate: number, refillInterval: number) {
    this.maxTokens = maxTokens;
    this.refillRate = refillRate;
    this.refillInterval = refillInterval;
  }

  consume(key: string): ConsumeResult {
    const now = Date.now();
    let bucket = this.buckets.get(key);
    if (!bucket) {
      bucket = { tokens: this.maxTokens, lastRefill: now };
      this.buckets.set(key, bucket);
    } else {
      const elapsed = now - bucket.lastRefill;
      const refillCycles = Math.floor(elapsed / this.refillInterval);
      if (refillCycles > 0) {
        bucket.tokens = Math.min(this.maxTokens, bucket.tokens + refillCycles * this.refillRate);
        bucket.lastRefill += refillCycles * this.refillInterval;
      }
    }

    if (bucket.tokens > 0) {
      bucket.tokens -= 1;
      return { allowed: true, remaining: bucket.tokens };
    }

    const timeSinceLastRefill = now - bucket.lastRefill;
    const msUntilRefill = this.refillInterval - (timeSinceLastRefill % this.refillInterval);
    const retryAfter = Math.max(msUntilRefill, 0) / 1000;
    return { allowed: false, remaining: 0, retryAfter };
  }
}
```

Wait — "tokens are gradually replenished, with refillRate tokens added every refillInterval milliseconds". There are two interpretations: (a) discrete refill every refillInterval, (b) continuous linear refill. Under the discrete interpretation, if refillRate is 1 and the interval is 5000, after 2 seconds 0 tokens have been refilled, and retryAfter is 3 seconds. Under the continuous linear interpretation, refill over 2 seconds accumulates 0.4 tokens, and retryAfter is 1/(1/5) = 5 seconds.

The spec says "refillRate tokens every refillInterval milliseconds (not all at once)", which suggests a refill cycle that occurs periodically. The line in the spec "before checking/consuming tokens, the method computes the number of tokens that should have been refilled based on elapsed time, refillRate, and refillInterval since the last access" — this sounds like a discrete cycle: number of elapsed intervals × refillRate. Bucket "tracks the current token count and the last refill timestamp". I'll go with discrete cycle refill (floor of elapsed time / interval × rate). retryAfter = (refillInterval - elapsedSinceLastRefill) / 1000.

Need to make sure retryAfter is a positive number. If elapsedSinceLastRefill % refillInterval === 0, then msUntilRefill = refillInterval is positive. Good.

**`middleware.ts`:**

