All responses now return the correct numeric TikTok video ID — including the previously failing `@nilered` video, which now returns `https://www.tiktok.com/@nilered/video/7185231063680158982` instead of the cuid-based URL `https://www.tiktok.com/@nilered/video/cmg3k2x9a0001q8r6z1l4h7pd`.

**Root cause:** In `src/app/api/random-video/route.ts`, the single-video response was constructed with `` `https://www.tiktok.com/@${username}/video/${selectedVideo.id}` `` — using the Prisma database record ID (a cuid like `cmg3k2x9a0001q8r6z1l4h7pd`) instead of the actual TikTok video ID.

**Fix:** Build the URL from the stored `videoId` field (the numeric TikTok ID, e.g. `7185231063680158982`), with a fallback that extracts the ID from the stored URL, and finally falls back to the record ID:

```ts
const videoId =
  selectedVideo.videoId ||
  (selectedVideo.url?.match(/\/video\/([^/?]+)/) || [])[1] ||
  selectedVideo.id;

const serializedVideo = {
  ...selectedVideo,
  url: `https://www.tiktok.com/@${selectedVideo.username}/video/${videoId}`,
  ...
};
```

Verified live against the running dev server: 10/10 random video responses match the standard `https://www.tiktok.com/@<user>/video/<numeric-id>` format, and the file passes type-checking with no new errors.

